{"name":"Big Band","hex":"#afaba0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"big band","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large dance or jazz band of 10 to 30 musicians usually featuring improvised solos by lead players, but otherwise playing orchestrated music.","The music produced by a jazz big band."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big_band"}],"entries":[{"title":"Big band","blocks":[{"text":"A big band is a type of musical ensemble of jazz music that usually consists of 10 or more musicians with four sections: saxophones, trumpets, trombones, and a rhythm section. Big bands originated during the early 1910s and dominated jazz in the early 1940s when swing was most popular. The term \"big band\" is also used to describe a genre of music, although this was not the only style of music played by big bands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Whitemanband1921.jpg/330px-Whitemanband1921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_band"},{"title":"Big Band (Charlie Parker album)","blocks":[{"text":"Big Band is a 1953 album by Charlie Parker of sides recorded in 1950 and 1952. In 1999 Big Band was reissued with bonus material and outtakes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/Charlie_Parker_Big_Band_Clef.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Band_(Charlie_Parker_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/US_Navy_071210-N-9860Y-002_Navy_Band_Northwest_%28NBNW%29_Big_Band%2C_%22Cascade%22%2C_plays_%22Holly_and_the_Ivy_-_God_Rest_Ye_Merry_Gentlemen%22_at_the_%22Holly%2C_Jolly_Holiday%22_concert_held_in_Parker_Hall_of_Oak_Harbor_High_School.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm